  "context_pill": "Capital Gains: Deemed Value & Improvement Rules",
  "example_summary": "Mr. C's property sale involves substituting the 1975 cost with the 2001 FMV (capped by SDV) and filtering out pre-2001 improvement costs.",
  "source_provision": "### Statutory Summary Matrix: Capital Gains Computation\n\n| Provision / Element | Statutory Section | Legal Rule & Threshold | Statutory Treatment / Restriction |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Full Value of Consideration** | Section 48 | Actual sale price realized upon transfer of capital asset | Reduced by actual expenses incurred exclusively in connection with transfer. |\n| **Cost of Acquisition (Pre-2001)** | Section 55(2)(b) | Option for assessee to take Fair Market Value as on 1st April 2001 | Cannot exceed the Stamp Duty Value of the asset as on 1st April 2001. |\n| **Cost of Improvement** | Section 55(1)(b) | Capital expenditure incurred by assessee in making additions or alterations | Strictly restricted to improvements incurred on or after 1st April 2001. |\n\n\n> [!IMPORTANT] Pre-2001 Improvement Restriction: Any capital expenditure incurred towards additions, alterations, or reconstruction of a capital asset prior to 1st April 2001 is completely ignored for the purpose of computing cost of improvement under Section 55(1)(b).\n\n\n> [!WARNING] Stamp Duty Value Cap: When substituting the Fair Market Value of a capital asset acquired before 1st April 2001, the adopted cost of acquisition cannot exceed the stamp duty value of that asset as on 1st April 2001, if available.",
